<title>UK: TENNIS-RECORD ENTRIES FOR 1998 DAVIS CUP.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-RECORD ENTRIES FOR 1998 DAVIS CUP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A record-breaking 131 nations will compete in the 1998 Davis Cup, the International Tennis Federation said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>First-time entries Honduras, Netherlands Antilles, St. Lucia and the U.S. Virgin Islands were accepted to join the 127 nations which took part in the 1997 Davis Cup.</p>
<p>The semifinal round of this year's competition, to be held from September 19 to 21, pits the United States again Australia in the U.S. capital Washington D.C. and Sweden against Italy in Norrkoping, Sweden.</p>
</text>
